<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Tahitian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1847</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Tahitian War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Tahitians loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-iv">Queen Pōmare</a> IV after Admiral Dupetit-Thouars imposed a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1842 and then deposed the queen. Tahitian fighters resisted from the mountains while the queen took refuge on Raiatea. After the French took the last strongholds in 1846, Pōmare IV returned in 1847 and accepted the protectorate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-tahitian-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Tahitian War" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sébastien Charles Giraud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prise_du_fort_de_Fautahua_%C3%A0_Tahiti,_17_d%C3%A9cembre_1846,_Charles_Giraud,_1855.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
